        "name": "decision-with-alternatives-and-consequences",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "The Decision section correctly states the policy in retry.sh: at most 5 attempts, exponential backoff of 1s, 2s, 4s and 8s, then exit 1; both named alternatives (retry forever, fail fast) are given with reasons; and the Consequences are honest on both sides (a bounded worker hold versus long outages still surfacing and no per-caller configuration). It loses points because the alternatives sit in Context already framed as 'ruled out', which partly pre-announces the outcome instead of describing the situation neutrally."
      },
